# Paths excluded from the anonymous submission bundle.
#
# Nothing here is deleted from the repository. This file drives
# tools/make_submission_bundle.py, which materialises a filtered copy for
# double-blind review. One glob per line; '#' starts a comment.
#
# The bar for exclusion is: a reviewer cannot reproduce any reported number
# with it, and removing it does not change any number they can reproduce.
# Anything ambiguous is KEPT -- a bundle that is slightly too large costs
# nothing, whereas a bundle missing a dependency is unreproducible.

# --- Considered and deliberately KEPT: ocm/evaluation/rahgm/ -----------------
# The RAHGM suite looks like separate work -- its own 1,500-write corpus,
# reviewer-minutes model, simulated analyst, and four experiments its __init__
# calls "§3-§4" -- and docs/discriminating_metric_design.md defers reviewer
# modelling "to the RAHGM paper where the reviewer models already exist".
#
# It is nonetheless NOT excluded, because it is not separable. Four of its
# modules are about OCMR, i.e. *this* paper's system: ocmr_arm, run_ocmr_arm,
# summarize_ocmr_arm, and audit (the OCMR quarantine audit, which
# docs/evaluation_methodology.md relies on for quarantine reconciliation).
# Their transitive closure pulls in replay -> corpus, metrics, review_cost, and
# audit -> annotate. That leaves only 10 of 20 modules droppable while corpus,
# metrics and review_cost would still ship, so excluding half the subsystem
# buys nothing and risks breaking the OCMR arm a reviewer may want to run.
#
# ocm/governance/{conditions,router}.py likewise keep their frozen_rahgm /
# adaptive_rahgm conditions (C4/C5): they live in a shared condition registry
# that this paper's gate also uses.

